ratorname{cos}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)] \\\\  & +[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}]+[1-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{12}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332762 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ecbfbfa-cec6-5df3-a0c9-e11c1f67b71c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e+1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330075} {:answer/id #uuid "4f85b6ee-800b-57ab-a844-ec6e2709c11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330672} {:answer/id #uuid "80f169d6-295c-563d-8914-8d2bd9999054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331093} {:answer/id #uuid "ba59d7eb-18ba-53f2-95b6-75daba77e7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331594} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1d4456-3d28-5aa2-8934-92baec9cfff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba59d7eb-18ba-53f2-95b6-75daba77e7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331594} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a4db82c-4c9f-5857-a947-4a090d21993d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "622f5ee2-fdb3-59b2-9462-4de78b4bcda0" :question/math-academy-id "q-49677" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral  $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{1/2}x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}(x{e}^{2x}){|}_{0}^{1/2}-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x{e}^{2x}){|}_{0}^{1/2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(1/2)}-0\\cdot {e}^{2\\cdot 0}]-\\frac{1}{4}[{e}^{2(1/2)}-{e}^{2\\cdot 0}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{e}{2}-0]-\\frac{1}{4}[e-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{4}-\\frac{e-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{e-e+1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2314e2c3-071d-5d1e-bdca-e7896981bcd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330252} {:answer/id #uuid "79f50141-9381-5317-8323-d88e90e3a8a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331031} {:answer/id #uuid "8b21378b-3425-5e03-a842-b62254df4ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331184} {:answer/id #uuid "b85d4fc1-2e09-58f6-acfa-bed34a4d5787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331579} {:answer/id #uuid "c25d6949-0735-57ba-84b8-0d9c36850ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25d6949-0735-57ba-84b8-0d9c36850ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331676} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe032e0-af40-56ec-a6ec-e09e79cb742f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b98f2873-3564-5f19-a00b-95639d25a774" :question/math-academy-id "q-49682" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)] \\\\  & +2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)] \\\\  & =2[-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]+2[0-0] \\\\  & =2(-2\\pi )+0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c9bf20-8128-53fc-aa86-1964b815386d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339304} {:answer/id #uuid "4eeb7e5b-2acb-5ebe-ad55-584b08e3b9c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339845} {:answer/id #uuid "534af3da-95e9-55b2-aba8-6f4b454b8ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339896} {:answer/id #uuid "90dc551e-639b-50fc-9023-134528ddbdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340425} {:answer/id #uuid "c5917a7f-b9e8-5505-bca8-86a9c397ec2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eeb7e5b-2acb-5ebe-ad55-584b08e3b9c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339845} :answer-field/id #uuid "64dee0d1-0120-5112-8fc9-ab060cbba4c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6203036f-b82a-557b-b713-2351ced43cc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-74087" :question/problem "Calculate  $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d4e53ff-430e-5b10-b738-cd8dd3d0256b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339385} {:answer/id #uuid "4b9151d3-7fde-540f-b82e-0580c7384593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339807} {:answer/id #uuid "989f6c04-735e-50e5-8fdd-bb014b8275b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340506} {:answer/id #uuid "add28c3c-0b54-53af-97fb-51c4b2116412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340712} {:answer/id #uuid "f90418c6-311c-5a49-b4cf-0366851ed196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{6}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "add28c3c-0b54-53af-97fb-51c4b2116412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340712} :answer-field/id #uuid "0614f8dc-7023-5386-a910-5a8612abf41b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b94b38f3-a670-562e-93ec-c45c6d3b0d77" :question/math-academy-id "q-74088" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x+1\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e99b757-9d06-5cfc-8db6-a2492878332c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{10}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339262} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4fd180-d811-5662-8d7f-8cf39e6abded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339651} {:answer/id #uuid "73d61482-1a92-5fde-a598-f549899e13ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340154} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f2d102-e8a3-564e-981d-58e57522a465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340754} {:answer/id #uuid "da9ff3c8-cb06-5827-af7c-d34ff6bef005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73d61482-1a92-5fde-a598-f549899e13ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340154} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a2565c-7c88-5b3a-b2f9-3d057c775bea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "31ac68e1-bc05-5634-b712-63c327f4e3c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74090" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=10x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=10 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 10x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fea6d91-968c-5f4d-8499-0425dc5d7fe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(3x+2){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362862} {:answer/id #uuid "df58de38-7310-5f19-9844-03c75ef49b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362863} {:answer/id #uuid "f721fccd-de41-549f-b75e-093592b0c032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+4){e}^{3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362864} {:answer/id #uuid "7db9ef7b-e876-5195-b2bc-5e90b186c364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(4x-3){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362865} {:answer/id #uuid "cab8da55-0308-5e36-8634-1b58557947b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(4x-1){e}^{3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df58de38-7310-5f19-9844-03c75ef49b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362863} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bcef777-2395-5b4a-81aa-40676383c492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "bd0da194-e627-59a2-b874-56e9ce11e475" :question/math-academy-id "q-114291" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int (2x+1){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int (2x+1){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x+1\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (2x+1)\\cdot {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(2x+1)\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+1){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(2x+1){e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1){e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{9}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(6x+1){e}^{3x}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "364fe6cb-9d03-53ce-a165-42f5c54b95ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3e}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362869} {:answer/id #uuid "c21264c7-8089-52ce-9a48-6dad38c7f2ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362870} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9db4ec-3467-518d-a30c-e4d04ca7e957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362871} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b710cd-dff5-5c54-9db5-d82e41461d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362872} {:answer/id #uuid "c0fe8a21-d6a2-507f-9611-cdd51fb00208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0fe8a21-d6a2-507f-9611-cdd51fb00208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362873} :answer-field/id #uuid "08dd7829-9567-51b3-9a69-757f02b76b0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "65eb7d35-cf19-5d83-87df-2f6cd4fcb07e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114317" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{1/4}x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{4x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\int \\left(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}\\right)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/4}x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{1}{4}x{e}^{4x}|}_{0}^{1/4}-\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1/4}{e}^{4x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}x{e}^{4x}|}_{0}^{1/4}-{\\frac{1}{16}{e}^{4x}|}_{0}^{1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4(1/4)}-0\\cdot {e}^{4\\cdot 0}]-\\frac{1}{16}[{e}^{4(1/4)}-{e}^{4\\cdot 0}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\frac{e}{4}-0]-\\frac{1}{16}[e-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{16}-\\frac{e}{16}+\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362996 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba8cff6-a436-587b-947b-b845d40cdf1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362998} {:answer/id #uuid "0bf7139d-5b6a-513e-8c05-ea38b19064dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{2x}}{2}-\\frac{3x{e}^{2x}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362999} {:answer/id #uuid "1a22e02f-c34e-55ad-b5ee-acd29d97566a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363000} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c30e70-a737-5f41-9c71-a8d0f2188c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363001} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a00544-29af-5a0e-9dbd-8c18e64ae108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3c30e70-a737-5f41-9c71-a8d0f2188c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363001} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4e46148-8029-5a37-a794-c93ccb0b0139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "708f4971-ac44-5610-9dca-92afa6cd2300" :question/math-academy-id "q-12558" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x+5}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9775c1a1-be1f-5d4a-8b38-2b22b3877645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+5)}{3}+\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363005} {:answer/id #uuid "25af2b05-29e6-557b-85e3-77fd7abe9e44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363006} {:answer/id #uuid "91cb4a25-ae24-57be-8930-89439bfcd808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363007} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b7d50e-bf4c-5d3c-8f65-093e0d804de6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{9}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363008} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c244ca-ce7e-5f14-8b4e-fc2f90fec15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91cb4a25-ae24-57be-8930-89439bfcd808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363007} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5a6fdb-0204-5d6b-854a-5929492322cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6d889fae-ff07-5704-acc9-b1fed02f79be" :question/math-academy-id "q-12565" :question/problem "Calculate  $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}\\right)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31cdfcf9-98d2-5183-877d-c6911c5786e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364277} {:answer/id #uuid "0c65c166-229d-5e3b-933e-08d975e562bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364278} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2cde5a-f869-5481-8dc3-00dd3ad08d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364279} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d225f4-6349-507e-b1a7-f6934a27b132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364280} {:answer/id #uuid "23f19c4b-e2a1-55d9-989d-819c4ed4c37f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa2cde5a-f869-5481-8dc3-00dd3ad08d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364279} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce18f523-92fa-512f-8b3f-d199baff422a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6d40fd3d-7b15-59ca-8ee5-88d3927298a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-49678" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }12x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=12x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=12 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 12x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =12x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 12\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }12x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }+12{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-12[\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )] \\\\  & +12[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )] \\\\  & =-12[-\\pi -\\pi ]+12[0-0] \\\\  & =-12[-2\\pi ] \\\\  & =24\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b416a21d-f860-5ddd-9887-3909cbcfc268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367605} {:answer/id #uuid "84ff0b6d-4bc8-58b4-8c1f-7733a5d10ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367606} {:answer/id #uuid "8e61b06f-5796-5daf-a560-740f317dd6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{4}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367607} {:answer/id #uuid "52c4db08-6d75-5662-ba65-98e14935cb32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367608} {:answer/id #uuid "665ef108-98da-5b42-b5b6-51f12caa5073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84ff0b6d-4bc8-58b4-8c1f-7733a5d10ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367606} :answer-field/id #uuid "7906d722-793f-554d-8af3-30e86eebaf11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c948087e-b394-5663-8b66-c2d6a56d25e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-14451" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}\\right)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81ae3e78-b1f4-5477-8bac-c412eb3c2747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ae3e78-b1f4-5477-8bac-c412eb3c2747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431280} :answer-field/id #uuid "0902a00b-6972-5278-913c-8072ffb99155" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5473d4ab-39f5-5e1e-ade8-0e74627b89e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-349299" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=4 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 4x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =4x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 0)+4(0-1) \\\\  & =2\\pi -4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186582344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028844d9-7a8c-56cb-97b5-243615c48f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581857} {:answer/id #uuid "0412cc02-5e89-54af-9e0d-33a68b7882bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581859} {:answer/id #uuid "086e05ff-9e32-5d33-918e-db4913094b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581866} {:answer/id #uuid "74bb02be-d93c-55c3-a1dc-4ea153765530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582018} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f9412d-1939-5921-a40f-b7846de4c3be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "086e05ff-9e32-5d33-918e-db4913094b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581866} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1b40783-b3b1-5667-bfbf-c04807510d00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "03d6bd28-9137-58b1-a51f-323589876595" :question/math-academy-id "q-2426" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={sec}^{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ where $\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\int \\frac{1}{u}(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186582346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a029170d-186d-5e9b-a3a0-ec97e60f70e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582088} {:answer/id #uuid "27ed81b4-2392-4797-b02a-30f4902d42f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a029170d-186d-5e9b-a3a0-ec97e60f70e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582088} :answer-field/id #uuid "c896b72e-60ed-5200-bc81-6211a9af0c23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "04e878c4-ef9a-56f2-a94f-14ca4b6e3aa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-349241" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\pi x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2\\pi x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2\\pi  \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x) & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2\\pi x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\pi x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x))\\cdot 2\\pi \\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\pi x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2(1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0))+\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0)) \\\\  & =-2(-1-0)+\\frac{2}{\\pi }(0-0) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186582361 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01861aad-c2ed-560c-b194-0e766a54a9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581853} {:answer/id #uuid "2c2032da-f210-52c4-9898-9c4e6c8ce89d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{2}+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581912} {:answer/id #uuid "74cf991d-e275-5d7c-a8b6-7a9debcd2664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582019} {:answer/id #uuid "79cf1b35-884a-5f6e-b843-da1e7572ebe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}(2{e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582025} {:answer/id #uuid "7a8a2b58-858b-5ac1-9570-d6d442159759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74cf991d-e275-5d7c-a8b6-7a9debcd2664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582019} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6b6524-5691-59e1-8ba0-d30fe60e4b0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "34541a55-604c-506e-8ac8-848875379923" :question/math-academy-id "q-49680" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{1/2}4x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=4 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{4x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into  the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 4x\\cdot {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x. \\\\  & =x{e}^{4x}-\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}4x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={x{e}^{4x}|}_{0}^{1/2}-{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x{e}^{4x}|}_{0}^{1/2}-{\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4(1/2)}-0\\cdot {e}^{4\\cdot 0}]-\\frac{1}{4}[{e}^{4(1/2)}-{e}^{4\\cdot 0}] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}-0]-\\frac{1}{4}[{e}^{2}-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186582385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6da09ad6-c4f6-515f-98c1-f47ff573d6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582001} {:answer/id #uuid "b176f022-afe3-44a9-8e64-fcd4977c1c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6da09ad6-c4f6-515f-98c1-f47ff573d6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582001} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6bf5813-494b-5256-a892-01704f92231f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8b131b7d-3fa7-5599-8f01-aac8709d4baa" :question/math-academy-id "q-349276" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2(\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =2(0-0)+\\frac{2}{3}(-1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186582409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b554e5-67f5-59cc-b410-930af877330a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581881} {:answer/id #uuid "120160f0-0063-52a3-bcb3-6e68643ff806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581884} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf32d90-eb55-5cb6-bd84-8a7cc555ceef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581983} {:answer/id #uuid "adfe33aa-5eaf-5562-b5a2-6cf71f2466e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582112} {:answer/id #uuid "da6d045c-c0e4-5deb-99cd-c404c3cf45bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}+\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adfe33aa-5eaf-5562-b5a2-6cf71f2466e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582112} :answer-field/id #uuid "60a94088-6e0b-5425-b352-4fdea86a8ff4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ecef7e80-ec65-5fcc-bcee-fa246b15e720" :question/math-academy-id "q-14439" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{5x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{5x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608215 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15a61ad7-79c1-597e-b11c-19dd09903bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607829} {:answer/id #uuid "371c726f-d93e-535e-8a96-08a8cf95914f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}+\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607867} {:answer/id #uuid "e977e102-a296-5ad5-ac58-227bccc1a06d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608060} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1ae4d5-c8d6-5a8d-84e5-ae8b3f0a3d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608064} {:answer/id #uuid "fc91c68d-0d4b-50b6-a510-3e9c2f09fe7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15a61ad7-79c1-597e-b11c-19dd09903bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607829} :answer-field/id #uuid "18e8c34f-a0b9-520d-9f5e-f104314fae97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ad8a7bb6-4f28-5469-bc34-0461c89c315f" :question/math-academy-id "q-14454" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{6x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{6x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{1}{6}\\int {e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{36}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c48dd4b-db1e-5aca-a708-9c53f96b5c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5(2{e}^{3}+1)}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c48dd4b-db1e-5aca-a708-9c53f96b5c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5(2{e}^{3}+1)}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607924} :answer-field/id #uuid "a779df38-7a72-5f60-a56e-44e357815ee8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c270c805-bb9a-5905-914b-1f5a0872a942" :question/math-academy-id "q-349327" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{1}5x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=5 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{3x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 5x\\cdot {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5x\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}-\\int \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}5x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{3}x{e}^{3x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}-\\frac{5}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}x{e}^{3x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}-\\frac{5}{9}{e}^{3x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}({e}^{3}-0)-\\frac{5}{9}({e}^{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3}-\\frac{5}{9}({e}^{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5(2{e}^{3}+1)}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "120393bd-f6bf-542f-bd4b-48617262d79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac\\pi4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693794} {:answer/id #uuid "46d27e52-8ebd-535d-8c75-390088ae0270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac\\pi2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693798} {:answer/id #uuid "62c64977-ec46-5dd5-a2ce-6727bb70c073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac\\pi4+\\frac14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693800} {:answer/id #uuid "bbfeac0e-3f32-58e4-a809-2218e78e0a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac\\pi4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693804} {:answer/id #uuid "c3eaf698-f423-5b74-bf2b-8e639a46db1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbfeac0e-3f32-58e4-a809-2218e78e0a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac\\pi4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693804} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d795ae8-d38f-5b1e-9f09-596ad1795065" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3983ce3c-17a0-527c-b83a-700f3e8a900f" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral.\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/2} x\\sin(2x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose $u=x$ and $v'=\\sin(2x)$, so $u'=1$ and $v=-\\frac12\\cos(2x)$.\n\nSubstitute into the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI\n&=\\left[-\\frac{x\\cos(2x)}2\\right]_0^{\\pi/2}\n+\\frac12\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\cos(2x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n&=\\left[-\\frac{x\\cos(2x)}2+\\frac{\\sin(2x)}4\\right]_0^{\\pi/2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow substitute the upper limit and subtract the value at the lower limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI\n&=\\left(-\\frac{\\pi\\cos\\pi}{4}+\\frac{\\sin\\pi}{4}\\right)\n-\\left(0+\\frac{\\sin0}{4}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac\\pi4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere the remaining integral contributes zero; the nonzero boundary term determines the result."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693799 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14126911-dcb8-5a40-b464-e96163280061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\frac{x e^{2x}}2\\right]_0^1-\\frac12\\int_0^1e^{2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693795} {:answer/id #uuid "27784cd8-1de2-54ed-8ab2-27040e4e82c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\frac{x e^{2x}}2\\right]_0^1-\\int_0^1e^{2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693796} {:answer/id #uuid "86cbfb29-9294-5ea7-b122-5eaacf32979d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[x e^{2x}\\right]_0^1-\\frac12\\int_0^1e^{2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693801} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6a3bdf-4fe0-59ac-8471-0b612d7b24ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac12\\int_0^1e^{2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693807} {:answer/id #uuid "f7e75cb3-9faf-53b5-baab-c1e3ea09abb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\frac{x e^{2x}}2\\right]_0^1+\\frac12\\int_0^1e^{2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14126911-dcb8-5a40-b464-e96163280061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\frac{x e^{2x}}2\\right]_0^1-\\frac12\\int_0^1e^{2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693795} :answer-field/id #uuid "f58e8eba-9d31-502e-8334-8918dd161c45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "61a5a880-9d8d-5a0d-ae74-48cef90c5ec6" :question/problem "Apply integration by parts once to\n\n$$\n\\int_0^1 x e^{2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct rewrite with $u=x$ and $v'=e^{2x}$. Leave the remaining integral unevaluated." :question/worked-solution "With $u=x$ and $v'=e^{2x}$, we have $u'=1$ and $v=\\frac12 e^{2x}$. The factor $\\frac12$ is needed because the exponent has derivative $2$.\n\nUse the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv'\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu'\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_0^1 x e^{2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\left[\\frac{x e^{2x}}2\\right]_0^1-\\int_0^1\\frac{e^{2x}}2\\cdot1\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{x e^{2x}}2\\right]_0^1-\\frac12\\int_0^1e^{2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe boundary term and the remaining integral both retain the original limits. This is the requested rewrite."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693808 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a70b874d-eafa-57a5-9685-73abfcb42909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi+2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a70b874d-eafa-57a5-9685-73abfcb42909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi+2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693803} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdc54588-7661-5d57-a65a-7d30f7b4d76c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d6ccd625-6440-5c85-8383-7c7fa5be03c9" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2} x\\cos(2x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose $u=x$ and $v'=\\cos(2x)$. Then $u'=1$ and $v=\\frac12\\sin(2x)$.\n\nIntegration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI\n&=\\left[\\frac{x\\sin(2x)}2\\right]_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2}\n-\\frac12\\int_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2}\\sin(2x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{x\\sin(2x)}2+\\frac{\\cos(2x)}4\\right]_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $F(x)=\\frac{x\\sin(2x)}2+\\frac{\\cos(2x)}4$, the two endpoint values are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(\\pi/2)&=\\frac{\\pi\\sin\\pi}{4}+\\frac{\\cos\\pi}{4}=-\\frac14,\\\\\nF(\\pi/4)&=\\frac{\\pi\\sin(\\pi/2)}8+\\frac{\\cos(\\pi/2)}4=\\frac\\pi8.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtract the entire lower-endpoint value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I&=F(\\pi/2)-F(\\pi/4)\\\\&=-\\frac14-\\frac\\pi8\\\\&=-\\frac{\\pi+2}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth endpoints contribute. The negative result also agrees with $x>0$ and $\\cos(2x)<0$ inside the interval."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1b88c8-541c-545b-a454-3f5affa928b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 x \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+4 \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693907} {:answer/id #uuid "2700ad5e-c837-57d7-9341-d849c9444445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 x \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+\\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693912} {:answer/id #uuid "b670c128-0083-5d0f-9c92-82612640cdb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+16 \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693933} {:answer/id #uuid "d29936a2-f45e-5fbd-9efc-a20473250ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+4 \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693935} {:answer/id #uuid "f444d0ad-fb36-52b6-9869-6123ada215db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+\\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d29936a2-f45e-5fbd-9efc-a20473250ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+4 \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693935} :answer-field/id #uuid "990f8d6f-2215-560c-8003-41d5671230d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "091220e8-625c-54b0-9a64-91384f985f9f" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\int 4 x\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Write $I=\\int 4 x\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\,\\text{d}x$. Use integration by parts.\n\n$$\n\\int uv^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=uv-\\int vu^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nChoose the linear factor as $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =4 x \\\\ u^{\\prime} & =4 \\\\ v^{\\prime} & =\\operatorname{cos}(x) \\\\ v & =\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}uv & =4 x\\left(\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\right) \\\\ \\int vu^{\\prime}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\right)4\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =4 x\\operatorname{sin}(x)-4\\int \\operatorname{sin}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4 x\\operatorname{sin}(x)-4(-\\operatorname{cos}(x))+C \\\\  & =4 x\\operatorname{sin}(x)+4\\operatorname{cos}(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "176475d1-b4fd-5c1b-b37b-4ea09414f5c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+\\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693910} {:answer/id #uuid "3e75540c-cfee-52c6-830d-8b29a2e56a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+2 \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693915} {:answer/id #uuid "82fe6589-a7cc-5777-bb90-0cc9c2996954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+2 \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693924} {:answer/id #uuid "9940dcd0-f6fc-5366-b7bf-961090001817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}{(x )}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693929} {:answer/id #uuid "b1fd5684-ad5a-5490-a366-79ef9b1e5725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+\\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1fd5684-ad5a-5490-a366-79ef9b1e5725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+\\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693931} :answer-field/id #uuid "4afcc0bf-3aba-520e-b67a-aef0a5515c00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4bba3ad9-c1ce-5fc6-bb50-b500dd56f77b" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\int x\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Write $I=\\int x\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\,\\text{d}x$. Use integration by parts.\n\n$$\n\\int uv^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=uv-\\int vu^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nChoose the linear factor as $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x \\\\ u^{\\prime} & =1 \\\\ v^{\\prime} & =\\operatorname{sin}(x) \\\\ v & =-\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}uv & =x\\left(-\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\right) \\\\ \\int vu^{\\prime}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(-\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\right)1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-x\\operatorname{cos}(x)+\\int \\operatorname{cos}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}(x)+(\\operatorname{sin}(x))+C \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}(x)+\\operatorname{sin}(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fbf3b1f-1c20-54a0-aa8c-6a741efdce9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}- 6 \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693908} {:answer/id #uuid "24087e23-21eb-5cc0-952e-c5ae70c1d518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 36 x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+6 \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693911} {:answer/id #uuid "58c93266-5735-5b4f-ad40-a57b6e9b364e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}- 6 \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693919} {:answer/id #uuid "85a040f3-ce85-5fb8-a277-713c37815088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x \\operatorname{cos}{(x )}+6 \\operatorname{sin}{(x )}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693925} {:answer/id #uuid "ee162c45-a71f-530b-8e29-02