\\\\ u^{\\prime} & =2 \\\\ v^{\\prime} & =\\operatorname{csc}^{2}(x - 3) \\\\ v & =-\\operatorname{cot}(x - 3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}uv & =2 x\\left(-\\operatorname{cot}(x - 3)\\right) \\\\ \\int vu^{\\prime}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(-\\operatorname{cot}(x - 3)\\right)2\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $t=\\operatorname{sin}(x - 3)$ and $\\mathrm{d}t=\\operatorname{cos}(x - 3)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$. Evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-2 x\\operatorname{cot}(x - 3)+2\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}(x - 3)}{\\operatorname{sin}(x - 3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2 x\\operatorname{cot}(x - 3)+2\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2 x\\operatorname{cot}(x - 3)+2\\ln|t|+C \\\\  & =-2 x\\operatorname{cot}(x - 3)+2\\ln|\\operatorname{sin}(x - 3)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis holds on each interval where $\\operatorname{sin}(x - 3)\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2922c9f0-92c7-54aa-b1bc-8713a4829bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694028} {:answer/id #uuid "a91f861e-1477-5655-80de-a9676ba5d8d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694034} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ef433f-84e1-506c-8f77-806feacf3793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694036} {:answer/id #uuid "c7057f1c-d64e-518d-983a-9c268c127450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694038} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ef222b-dd03-50a1-8c94-937df7b854b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4ef433f-84e1-506c-8f77-806feacf3793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694036} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e67b05e-d437-52d1-bc23-e904ac4fa5f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4fe76186-1b66-54b0-8bb5-0af3ecb093f6" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} - 2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 2 x, & u^\\prime&=-2,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}, & v&=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[- x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}+\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[- x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=- \\frac{\\pi}{4}=- \\frac{\\pi}{4},\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{2}=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b14a21-47a1-57a4-8efd-8c016017e964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694027} {:answer/id #uuid "4a123331-319d-5bf4-9437-1f3e9365759b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694029} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a3ce10-ce3f-5369-8c33-2f3e15f51a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 + 3 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694035} {:answer/id #uuid "c9639572-738f-5a02-9440-796ed8d0e2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694039} {:answer/id #uuid "e7099de2-3375-5be9-9b3d-c7724a40ee2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a123331-319d-5bf4-9437-1f3e9365759b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694029} :answer-field/id #uuid "26b13cc2-2281-5a26-bcb5-4e2083e02a44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7c3f13b9-9f08-5abf-8bc4-09d3a8f9f34c" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} x e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=x, & u^\\prime&=1,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=e^{x}, & v&=e^{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{2}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[x e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{2}-\\int_{0}^{2}e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x e^{x} - e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(2\\right)&=e^{2}=e^{2},\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=-1=-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(e^{2}\\right)-\\left(-1\\right)\\\\\n&=1 + e^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694032 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0944a8c-e925-5838-a71e-185be5f7503c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3} + e^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0944a8c-e925-5838-a71e-185be5f7503c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3} + e^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694041} :answer-field/id #uuid "f91d6f08-6f6b-5092-908a-ffe4abacac55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "830106cb-221a-5579-b783-ed41c2699df3" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0} 3 x e^{3 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=3 x, & u^\\prime&=3,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=e^{3 x}, & v&=\\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x e^{3 x}\\right]_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}\\left(\\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}\\right)\\left(3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[x e^{3 x}\\right]_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}-\\int_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}e^{3 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x e^{3 x} - \\frac{e^{3 x}}{3}\\right]_{- \\frac{2}{3}}^{0}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(0\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{3}=- \\frac{1}{3},\\\\\nF\\left(- \\frac{2}{3}\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{e^{2}}=- \\frac{1}{e^{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{e^{2}}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{1}{3} + e^{-2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694033 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbace438-7b69-5b06-b987-e0b80fbdb22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{9} - \\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbace438-7b69-5b06-b987-e0b80fbdb22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{9} - \\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694037} :answer-field/id #uuid "120534b4-87f2-51ea-a712-8c3d27135e88" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9f41da68-af7f-5236-903f-45ebee73bc95" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} 2 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=2 x, & u^\\prime&=2,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}, & v&=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{2 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right)\\left(2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{2 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{2 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3} + \\frac{2 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{9}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)&=- \\frac{2}{9}=- \\frac{2}{9},\\\\\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)&=\\frac{\\pi}{9}=\\frac{\\pi}{9}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{2}{9}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{9}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{\\pi}{9} - \\frac{2}{9}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12019bb2-d918-52a1-95c3-e42fd160a1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12019bb2-d918-52a1-95c3-e42fd160a1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694023} :answer-field/id #uuid "defce1ab-2273-5db1-9cd7-8ea709917a8b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ca39675d-730b-5c00-8b6e-0a1fa354e304" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\pi} - 2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 2 x, & u^\\prime&=-2,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}, & v&=- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\pi}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\pi}-\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\pi}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\pi\\right)&=\\pi=\\pi,\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=0=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(\\pi\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=\\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694056 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "235b0043-f42f-517c-b76c-0c6c5957735b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694053} {:answer/id #uuid "41ecaa1d-f654-59d8-b849-303d53533faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694058} {:answer/id #uuid "4dd3f94a-d93b-54ba-aac8-7c1ad4eed67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694060} {:answer/id #uuid "52220479-eb3e-51eb-92dc-ca5be80a0098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694062} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0f9b08-70f4-51fb-b872-dbdbefe770b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "235b0043-f42f-517c-b76c-0c6c5957735b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694053} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a29a93-96da-527c-b7ef-e9f4430f4c9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "30c5211d-64de-5dea-aef8-9c40edc08734" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - 3 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $I$ denote the given integral. Choose the factors so that differentiating the linear factor simplifies the remaining integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 3 x, & u^\\prime&=-3,\\\\\nv^\\prime&=\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}, & v&=- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the definite integration-by-parts formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b uv^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x=[uv]_a^b-\\int_a^b vu^\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{3 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\\\\n&\\quad-\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x,\\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{3 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}-\\frac{3}{2}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the remaining function and combine the two primitive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left[\\frac{3 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)$ denote the primitive inside the brackets. Evaluate each endpoint, then subtract the entire lower value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4},\\\\\nF\\left(0\\right)&=0=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI&=\\left(- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00efb0ca-1dce-55b8-afef-dc0d016dd030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694047} {:answer/id #uuid "0dfb4527-b8d2-57bc-994b-9ebf97f12e24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860